<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SpotBugs exclude filter. Three narrow, documented exclusions only — no category-wide rule is
  disabled:

  1. EI_EXPOSE_REP/EI_EXPOSE_REP2 on the internal raw-bytes HTTP response body ({@code
     ApiResponse}). Carrying the actual bytes rather than a defensive copy is the intended contract;
     the payload can be large (dataset exports, records ZIPs) and copying it on every access would be
     wasteful. {@code ApiResponse} lives in the internal package (not user-facing). The user-facing
     {@code KeyValueStoreRecord} value type does defensively copy its bytes. All other
     representation-exposure warnings are fixed in code (unmodifiable getters / copy-on-set).

  2. UWF_UNWRITTEN_FIELD / UWF_UNWRITTEN_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD on KeyValueStoreKey and
     ApiErrorEnvelope (and its nested Body): Jackson-populated DTOs whose fields are written by the
     deserializer via reflection, which SpotBugs cannot see — a known false positive for
     data-binding models.

  3. EI_EXPOSE_REP2 on ActorClient/RunClient/TaskClient storing the {@code ApifyClient} passed to
     their constructor (as {@code root}, used to reach sibling resources, e.g. a run's Actor). Since
     the package split introduced by this change, these constructors are public (Java requires
     cross-package visibility for ApifyClient, in the root package, to construct resource clients
     that now live in their own sub-packages) — SpotBugs only flags representation exposure through
     reachable (public) constructors, so this finding is new to this change, not a regression in
     behavior. It is a false positive, not a real defect: `ApifyClient` is an effectively-immutable
     facade (a final HTTP client plus two final base-URL strings, no mutator methods whatsoever), so
     there is no caller-reachable way to mutate a `root` reference after construction, and defensively
     copying it would be meaningless (it is not a value/data object) as well as wasteful.
-->
<FindBugsFilter>
  <Match>
    <Class name="com.apify.client.internal.ApiResponse"/>
    <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
  </Match>
  <Match>
    <Class name="com.apify.client.keyvalue.KeyValueStoreKey"/>
    <Bug pattern="UWF_UNWRITTEN_FIELD"/>
  </Match>
  <Match>
    <Or>
      <Class name="com.apify.client.internal.ApiErrorEnvelope"/>
      <Class name="com.apify.client.internal.ApiErrorEnvelope$Body"/>
    </Or>
    <Bug pattern="UWF_UNWRITTEN_FIELD,UWF_UNWRITTEN_PUBLIC_OR_PROTECTED_FIELD"/>
  </Match>
  <Match>
    <Or>
      <Class name="com.apify.client.actor.ActorClient"/>
      <Class name="com.apify.client.run.RunClient"/>
      <Class name="com.apify.client.task.TaskClient"/>
    </Or>
    <Field name="root"/>
    <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
  </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
